# A contact sheet of the stack marks, rendered by scripts/render-stack-marks.mjs so the
# eighteen logos can be eyeballed at their real 14px size. It is a thing to look at
# while working, not a thing to ship: the marks themselves live in client.js, and the
# check that every stack has one is scripts/check-detection.mjs.
assets/.stack-marks-check.png

# Animated GIFs are not stored here.
#
# GIF stores every frame as a complete bitmap with no inter-frame compression, so a
# ten-second clip that is 1.6 MB as video becomes 30 MB as GIF — twenty times the size
# for a worse-looking result. `assets/demo.mp4` carries the same clip at the smaller
# size and IS committed, deliberately: it is the fallback for anyone who cannot play
# the GitHub attachment, and 1.6 MB is a reasonable thing for a clone to carry.
#
#   git check-ignore -v assets/demo.mp4   # must NOT match
assets/*.gif
assets/*.mov
assets/*.mkv

# The superseded Chrome-extension implementation. It stays on the machines that
# already have it, but it is not part of this repository: the parts of it still
# worth reading live in docs/ (the element-fact collector and design notes).
legacy/
